1
00:00:06,173 --> 00:00:09,759
Uh, our info is limited,
these guys aren't in our database.

2
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:13,429
All we really know is that they came
from Guangzhou, China.

3
00:00:13,430 --> 00:00:15,891
I'm still investigating
to get the exact details.

4
00:00:16,475 --> 00:00:17,935
How close are we on the server?

5
00:00:18,435 --> 00:00:20,938
I still got, uh, two-thirds or more?

6
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:23,356
And the shopping mall migration?

7
00:00:23,357 --> 00:00:25,983
Seventy percent.
It's 'cause we're only working nights.

8
00:00:25,984 --> 00:00:28,445
We have to avoid any tracking by Babylon.

9
00:00:30,489 --> 00:00:31,949
I have to go get Jian myself.

10
00:00:33,408 --> 00:00:35,577
Those bastards are gonna
go after her quickly.

11
00:00:36,537 --> 00:00:37,621
What's that?

12
00:00:39,081 --> 00:00:40,207
I think they already found us.

13
00:01:22,541 --> 00:01:23,834
Can't get a clear shot.

14
00:01:24,459 --> 00:01:25,876
Container's in the way.

15
00:01:25,877 --> 00:01:27,504
As expected.

16
00:01:28,714 --> 00:01:29,964
Hold your positions.

17
00:01:29,965 --> 00:01:31,216
We're going in.

18
00:01:32,092 --> 00:01:35,761
Listen carefully.
Put your personal grudge aside.

19
00:01:35,762 --> 00:01:38,181
Jeong Jinman has
to be captured alive. Translate.

20
00:01:43,103 --> 00:01:45,938
Jeong Jinman needs
to be captured alive, sir.

21
00:01:45,939 --> 00:01:47,357
He has to be alive.

22
00:01:49,943 --> 00:01:51,987
Just don't get in my way.

23
00:01:53,488 --> 00:01:56,866
You'll die first. Translate.

24
00:01:56,867 --> 00:01:58,035
Ah, shit.

25
00:02:00,537 --> 00:02:03,123
Uh… what he said was…

26
00:02:03,623 --> 00:02:05,584
Ah, die first?

27
00:02:06,752 --> 00:02:08,336
I didn't get the last part.

28
00:02:08,337 --> 00:02:09,796
What?

29
00:02:13,884 --> 00:02:15,469
That… one-eyed bastard…

30
00:02:33,236 --> 00:02:34,696
Appreciate you working so late.

31
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:43,038
We can begin now.

32
00:02:43,538 --> 00:02:50,545
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

33
00:02:54,549 --> 00:02:57,469
EPISODE 04
RAID

34
00:02:58,178 --> 00:02:59,179
Understood.

35
00:02:59,721 --> 00:03:02,723
I will retrieve the asset
and put things back in order.

36
00:03:17,948 --> 00:03:18,949
Who is it?

37
00:03:19,408 --> 00:03:22,451
Who could make the great Kusanagi act
so submissively, huh?

38
00:03:24,955 --> 00:03:29,792
I can keep on climbing higher and higher,
but there's always another level.

39
00:03:31,211 --> 00:03:32,546
Don't you miss fieldwork?

40
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:34,381
Not at all.

41
00:03:35,090 --> 00:03:36,507
The smell of blood…

42
00:03:37,634 --> 00:03:39,885
…and gunpowder just stays in your nose.

43
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:40,887
Ugh.

44
00:03:43,056 --> 00:03:45,183
I'd rather be a knight than a pawn anyway.

45
00:03:46,184 --> 00:03:50,105
Or even better, I could be the one
who designs the board in the first place.

46
00:03:57,112 --> 00:04:00,323
As for capturing Jeong Jinman,
you need to be the one to do it.

47
00:04:04,202 --> 00:04:05,454
I like the sound of that.

48
00:04:07,581 --> 00:04:08,582
And Q?

49
00:04:09,583 --> 00:04:10,708
Q will…

50
00:04:13,753 --> 00:04:14,838
…get rattled.

51
00:04:16,256 --> 00:04:19,301
I need the one who leads this team
to be someone cold.

52
00:04:21,303 --> 00:04:22,429
Hmm…

53
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:27,267
Women's intuition.

54
00:05:25,867 --> 00:05:26,951
Smoke!

55
00:05:26,952 --> 00:05:28,662
Don't panic. Hold your positions.

56
00:05:44,135 --> 00:05:46,804
He's the most skilled agent
in your team.

57
00:05:46,805 --> 00:05:49,640
Don't you think it's long overdue
for J to lead a unit?

58
00:05:49,641 --> 00:05:53,854
I don't think it's combat skills
that determines a good leader.

59
00:05:56,690 --> 00:05:58,899
If the target's Jeong Jinman,
I think it does.

60
00:05:58,900 --> 00:05:59,901
That's not it.

61
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:03,738
I'm talking about Bale.

62
00:06:08,118 --> 00:06:10,244
Bale's just a hunting dog at this point.

63
00:06:10,245 --> 00:06:13,330
If you take him off his leash,
he'll find Jinman for us.

64
00:06:13,331 --> 00:06:14,708
We should be using that.

65
00:06:32,058 --> 00:06:36,605
Working with Bale to capture Jinman
was actually J's choice as team leader.

66
00:06:37,272 --> 00:06:40,025
You can't keep coddling him forever
because he's your little brother.

67
00:06:40,567 --> 00:06:41,860
J has the skills he needs.

68
00:06:48,033 --> 00:06:49,284
Branch Chief…

69
00:06:53,371 --> 00:06:55,498
are you and my brother
still seeing each other?

70
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:06,343
Heavy radio signal detected.

71
00:07:08,178 --> 00:07:09,387
Remove it.

72
00:07:10,347 --> 00:07:12,265
If you really cared about Jun…

73
00:07:13,975 --> 00:07:16,645
why stick him with a time bomb like Bale…

74
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:20,023
and send him after Jeong Jinman?

75
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:23,692
If you're afraid of things like that,

76
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:25,779
you're in the wrong line of work entirely.

77
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:29,574
You should try going back
to being yakuza again.

78
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:32,242
Or open a bar in Dotonbori

79
00:07:32,243 --> 00:07:34,412
and leave the dangerous missions to us.

80
00:07:48,843 --> 00:07:50,720
Hey, Japanese.

81
00:07:52,681 --> 00:07:55,183
-  It's a trap.
- What?

82
00:07:56,351 --> 00:07:58,520
If they hid the server
in a place like this,

83
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:02,148
wouldn't it mean they're prepared
to bolt at any moment?

84
00:08:06,945 --> 00:08:08,487
What are you doing?

85
00:08:08,488 --> 00:08:09,531
Translate it.

86
00:08:10,949 --> 00:08:12,658
If they hid the server
in a place like this,

87
00:08:12,659 --> 00:08:14,827
wouldn't it mean they're prepared
to bolt at any moment?

88
00:08:14,828 --> 00:08:15,954
That's what he's said.

89
00:08:21,251 --> 00:08:22,626
Bravo, Tango,

90
00:08:22,627 --> 00:08:23,836
find dead ends of containers

91
00:08:23,837 --> 00:08:26,548
that can be connected
to the current Alpha position,

92
00:08:27,048 --> 00:08:30,217
and identify all trucks, cranes,
and modes of transportation

93
00:08:30,218 --> 00:08:31,886
within a 100-meter radius.

94
00:08:32,512 --> 00:08:34,764
Possible ambush on Tango.

95
00:08:35,515 --> 00:08:37,851
J, forget about Tango.

96
00:08:40,311 --> 00:08:43,064
Hey, didn't you say it was a trap?

97
00:08:44,899 --> 00:08:46,568
What are you doing? Translate it.

98
00:08:49,237 --> 00:08:51,239
Hey, didn't you say it was a trap?

99
00:08:53,241 --> 00:08:56,411
If it's a trap, we don't go in?

100
00:08:58,413 --> 00:08:59,539
Are you scared?

101
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:03,543
Are you scared?

102
00:09:13,428 --> 00:09:17,598
That's right, the enemy of my enemy
should be my friend.

103
00:09:59,015 --> 00:10:00,141
After you.

104
00:10:07,148 --> 00:10:08,358
Grenade!

105
00:10:22,872 --> 00:10:24,874
Marco. Marco!

106
00:10:36,761 --> 00:10:37,928
I'm okay.

107
00:10:43,893 --> 00:10:45,060
I'll be right back.

108
00:10:47,689 --> 00:10:49,774
Jinman's here, that slick fuck.

109
00:10:59,576 --> 00:11:01,702
Bravo, current location?

110
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:17,385
After you.

111
00:11:40,950 --> 00:11:41,951
It's a trap.

112
00:13:00,613 --> 00:13:01,989
That hurts!

113
00:13:10,999 --> 00:13:12,041
Shit.

114
00:13:23,761 --> 00:13:25,846
Long time, no see.

115
00:13:25,847 --> 00:13:27,473
Jeong Jinman.

116
00:13:30,310 --> 00:13:33,020
I'm just sorry we have to meet like this.

117
00:13:33,021 --> 00:13:34,521
J, don't forget.

118
00:13:34,522 --> 00:13:36,482
We need Jeong Jinman alive.

119
00:13:58,713 --> 00:13:59,964
What the hell's that moron doing?

120
00:14:02,008 --> 00:14:04,218
I told you we have to capture him alive!

121
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:18,231
I thought I made it clear to you.

122
00:14:18,232 --> 00:14:20,525
If you get in my way, you'll die first.

123
00:14:43,174 --> 00:14:44,175
Shit.

124
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:52,433
Ugh…

125
00:15:00,650 --> 00:15:01,651
Move it.

126
00:15:11,077 --> 00:15:12,203
Shit.

127
00:15:27,969 --> 00:15:29,971
Look! Over there!

128
00:15:47,613 --> 00:15:49,406
Snipers, what are you doing?

129
00:15:49,407 --> 00:15:52,659
Hurry up and stop that truck.
Move to ten o'clock now!

130
00:16:15,808 --> 00:16:17,852
We're out of time, let's haul ass!

131
00:16:22,857 --> 00:16:25,610
You always did have something up
your sleeve, Jinman.

132
00:16:27,904 --> 00:16:29,530
Always so petty.

133
00:17:11,948 --> 00:17:13,281
Just ram through it!

134
00:17:13,282 --> 00:17:14,867
Hold on to something!

135
00:18:13,259 --> 00:18:14,969
All these clever little tricks

136
00:18:15,511 --> 00:18:18,179
are only gonna blow up in your face.

137
00:19:10,191 --> 00:19:14,027
Jeong Jinman, I'll see you in hell--

138
00:19:45,810 --> 00:19:47,185
Tell me,

139
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:49,354
are we being recorded
in the command center?

140
00:19:49,355 --> 00:19:50,605
No, ma'am.

141
00:19:50,606 --> 00:19:53,067
We don't record
unofficial internal operations.

142
00:19:55,111 --> 00:19:56,696
Good work, everybody.

143
00:19:57,488 --> 00:19:58,614
You can all go home.

144
00:20:05,162 --> 00:20:07,122
Q's operation is in a few hours.

145
00:20:07,123 --> 00:20:08,373
What's our angle here?

146
00:20:08,374 --> 00:20:09,457
Hmm…

147
00:20:09,458 --> 00:20:10,710
I'll figure something out.

148
00:20:11,419 --> 00:20:13,087
I'm starving.

149
00:20:18,676 --> 00:20:19,802
Can you handle it?

150
00:20:44,577 --> 00:20:46,119
Can I get room service?

151
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:49,290
Even though Bale's a psycho,
how could he kill his own team like that?

152
00:20:50,207 --> 00:20:52,501
Dying like a dog as soon
as you leave Japan…

153
00:20:53,210 --> 00:20:55,421
I heard that J was Q's younger brother.

154
00:21:15,816 --> 00:21:16,984
That hurts!

155
00:21:32,917 --> 00:21:34,835
- Yeah?
-  Everything is set.

156
00:21:35,377 --> 00:21:37,670
But there are two employees
from another department

157
00:21:37,671 --> 00:21:39,088
and the bus driver on board.

158
00:21:41,467 --> 00:21:42,843
I think that…

159
00:21:44,261 --> 00:21:46,596
looks more natural, don't you think?

160
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:57,649
Whoo!

161
00:21:57,650 --> 00:21:59,317
Good job, K.

162
00:22:07,827 --> 00:22:08,911
You understand?

163
00:22:09,620 --> 00:22:12,038
Jeong Jinman was the one who killed J.

164
00:22:12,039 --> 00:22:13,374
Bale didn't do it.

165
00:22:14,416 --> 00:22:16,918
We have to make sure
that Q never discovers the truth

166
00:22:16,919 --> 00:22:18,963
under any circumstances.

167
00:22:20,548 --> 00:22:23,551
This… stays between us.

168
00:22:41,110 --> 00:22:43,737
Fortunately,
the residents had all left the island.

169
00:22:44,405 --> 00:22:47,741
Your friend Miss Arin rushed to Seoul
because of her uncle's sudden passing.

170
00:22:48,325 --> 00:22:50,578
And it looks like she won't be able
to come back.

171
00:22:51,787 --> 00:22:53,663
We'll make it
so nothing happened here tonight.

172
00:22:53,664 --> 00:22:56,457
So, as long as you keep quiet,
that's the end of it.

173
00:22:56,458 --> 00:22:58,710
You'll be free to return
to your normal life.

174
00:22:58,711 --> 00:23:00,003
However,

175
00:23:00,004 --> 00:23:02,964
once Miss Jian leaves here,
you'll be strangers from that moment on.

176
00:23:02,965 --> 00:23:04,173
Any contact is forbidden.

177
00:23:04,174 --> 00:23:05,718
Hey, I don't think that's necess…

178
00:23:07,720 --> 00:23:09,221
That's going too far.

179
00:23:11,807 --> 00:23:13,057
Woojin…

180
00:23:17,771 --> 00:23:21,025
If you need help,
you can contact me at this number.

181
00:23:22,610 --> 00:23:24,820
CO., Ltd. JAEWON CLEANING
Team Leader Kim Jaewon

182
00:23:55,434 --> 00:23:56,435
Arin…

183
00:23:58,228 --> 00:23:59,438
No.

184
00:24:00,940 --> 00:24:02,232
Your real name is…

185
00:24:04,318 --> 00:24:05,778
Jian, isn't it?

186
00:24:16,372 --> 00:24:18,457
I don't think
I'll be any help cleaning here.

187
00:24:20,459 --> 00:24:21,961
Let me know when it's all done.

188
00:24:24,296 --> 00:24:25,547
I'll be at the house.

189
00:24:29,218 --> 00:24:30,469
Woojin, wait.

190
00:25:08,924 --> 00:25:11,593
Do you think it's okay to let him leave,
just like that?

191
00:25:12,761 --> 00:25:15,431
There are traces of him
having accessed the app data.

192
00:25:26,191 --> 00:25:29,319
When you catch up, what are you gonna say?

193
00:25:53,260 --> 00:25:54,470
That boy Woojin…

194
00:25:55,637 --> 00:25:56,680
do you like him?

195
00:26:01,769 --> 00:26:03,311
Stay level-headed.

196
00:26:03,312 --> 00:26:05,314
You remember Bae Jeongmin, right?

197
00:26:05,898 --> 00:26:08,692
- We don't know who'll come looking and--
-  Unni…

198
00:26:09,526 --> 00:26:10,861
I'm really hungry.

199
00:26:15,699 --> 00:26:17,451
Why don't we eat something?

200
00:26:18,077 --> 00:26:19,660
We got some mumallaengi.

201
00:26:19,661 --> 00:26:22,955
Auntie Soonae grows the radishes,
dries and seasons them herself.

202
00:26:22,956 --> 00:26:24,124
It's so good.

203
00:26:24,917 --> 00:26:28,212
And these are bangiip muchin and myeolchi
that Auntie Pilsun made.

204
00:26:28,837 --> 00:26:29,921
And this one…

205
00:26:31,840 --> 00:26:35,343
Auntie Jeomrye, she found out
I liked sausage and stir-fried vegetables,

206
00:26:35,344 --> 00:26:36,512
so she made this for me.

207
00:26:37,054 --> 00:26:38,596
Ah…

208
00:26:38,597 --> 00:26:39,932
Meongge-jeot…

209
00:26:40,516 --> 00:26:42,226
Auntie Jeomrye's specialty.

210
00:26:52,528 --> 00:26:53,529
Jian,

211
00:26:54,696 --> 00:26:56,824
we don't have time to be doing this.

212
00:27:03,163 --> 00:27:04,248
This stuff…

213
00:27:08,335 --> 00:27:09,419
I've never…

214
00:27:11,588 --> 00:27:14,173
I never got to just be like this
with Uncle.

215
00:27:21,932 --> 00:27:23,267
After getting here…

216
00:27:24,268 --> 00:27:27,980
living a normal life like everyone else,
it was just really nice.

217
00:27:29,231 --> 00:27:30,941
Having someone there for me…

218
00:27:32,734 --> 00:27:34,611
and me being there for them too.

219
00:27:36,947 --> 00:27:38,282
Laughing together,

220
00:27:39,366 --> 00:27:40,450
making meals,

221
00:27:41,243 --> 00:27:42,286
just talking…

222
00:27:44,621 --> 00:27:45,664
normal.

223
00:27:48,292 --> 00:27:50,002
A normal life, you know?

224
00:27:56,800 --> 00:28:00,219
Living a normal life
like everyone else gets to.

225
00:28:04,725 --> 00:28:06,351
Until yesterday, I really…

226
00:28:08,395 --> 00:28:10,856
…really believed
I could keep going like this.

227
00:28:11,982 --> 00:28:13,609
Look, your uncle really tried.

228
00:28:14,276 --> 00:28:16,527
He did everything he could for you, Jian.

229
00:28:16,528 --> 00:28:18,446
I know he did. I know that.

230
00:28:26,204 --> 00:28:29,207
I found a way here
to live life on my own terms.

231
00:28:30,292 --> 00:28:33,920
It's better than that cage he kept me in
'cause it was dangerous.

232
00:28:33,921 --> 00:28:36,048
And that was his past catching up to us.

233
00:28:37,007 --> 00:28:39,050
It had nothing at all to do with me.

234
00:28:43,221 --> 00:28:44,348
Even still…

235
00:28:46,350 --> 00:28:50,145
if you were to stay here,
Woojin and everyone around you

236
00:28:50,812 --> 00:28:52,147
will all be in danger.

237
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:56,151
I know that.

238
00:29:03,533 --> 00:29:05,661
I'll go back to my uncle, I just…

239
00:29:12,125 --> 00:29:13,168
Could we just…

240
00:29:16,254 --> 00:29:17,546
have one moment?

241
00:29:20,258 --> 00:29:22,678
Can we have one more meal
as normal people first?

242
00:30:24,406 --> 00:30:26,282
WOOJIN

243
00:30:59,274 --> 00:31:01,943
Team Leader, she isn't alone.
How should we handle this?

244
00:31:02,819 --> 00:31:04,612
You can eliminate anyone
who gets in your way.

245
00:31:04,613 --> 00:31:05,614
Just get her.

246
00:31:36,812 --> 00:31:38,604
And for our extraction?

247
00:31:38,605 --> 00:31:40,315
We can transport you on our ship.

248
00:31:43,110 --> 00:31:44,193
This is bad.

249
00:31:44,194 --> 00:31:45,319
You have to go now!

250
00:31:55,997 --> 00:31:58,500
Woojin, is there another way to the docks?

251
00:31:59,042 --> 00:32:01,168
On the back side of the island,
there's a way there.

252
00:32:01,169 --> 00:32:02,294
Listen carefully.

253
00:32:02,295 --> 00:32:04,463
I'll stay and stall them as long as I can.

254
00:32:04,464 --> 00:32:06,174
Head to the docks with Woojin.

255
00:32:06,716 --> 00:32:09,427
Once you get down there,
find the boat called the JW.

256
00:32:10,720 --> 00:32:12,012
Director Kim, give them cover.

257
00:32:12,013 --> 00:32:13,348
Right. I'm on it.

258
00:32:25,819 --> 00:32:26,820
Unni.

259
00:32:32,951 --> 00:32:34,077
I'll be fine.

260
00:32:34,828 --> 00:32:38,039
Listen, your unni will never die.

261
00:33:05,734 --> 00:33:06,860
They're coming!

262
00:34:11,424 --> 00:34:15,135
Team Leader, there's a four-wheeler
headed towards the docks.

263
00:34:15,136 --> 00:34:16,471
It looks like Jeong Jian.

264
00:34:23,520 --> 00:34:25,562
Bravo, start making your way in.

265
00:34:25,563 --> 00:34:26,564
Let's roll out.

266
00:35:46,645 --> 00:35:47,728
Are you all right?

267
00:35:51,941 --> 00:35:53,901
We have to hurry and catch up to Jian.

268
00:36:02,243 --> 00:36:03,370
Woojin!

269
00:37:19,654 --> 00:37:20,989
Arin, hold on to me!

270
00:38:35,980 --> 00:38:37,190
Arin…

271
00:38:55,708 --> 00:38:57,167
Arin, get up.

272
00:38:58,545 --> 00:39:00,129
Jeong Jian…

273
00:39:04,217 --> 00:39:07,302
Wait, is that your boat over there?

274
00:39:15,270 --> 00:39:16,729
You can't!

275
00:39:20,525 --> 00:39:21,608
Shit.

276
00:39:23,027 --> 00:39:24,904
This is your last chance.

277
00:39:30,368 --> 00:39:34,496
If you don't come with me, your boyfriend
will also die just like that.

278
00:40:10,283 --> 00:40:11,575
Hey, my boat's right there.

279
00:41:30,113 --> 00:41:31,489
You're her, huh?

280
00:41:32,699 --> 00:41:34,117
So Minhye.

281
00:42:17,410 --> 00:42:19,202
Woojin, hard left now!

282
00:43:06,626 --> 00:43:07,668
Seal it off.

283
00:43:53,589 --> 00:43:54,757
I'm sorry, Woojin.

284
00:44:01,973 --> 00:44:03,182
I'm doing fine.

285
00:44:03,975 --> 00:44:05,643
Look, I'm still in one piece.

286
00:44:06,936 --> 00:44:07,979
So don't worry.

287
00:44:12,191 --> 00:44:13,734
Hey, don't say you forgot,

288
00:44:14,610 --> 00:44:17,028
do you remember my promise?

289
00:44:17,029 --> 00:44:18,156
In Hanam-do.

290
00:44:18,990 --> 00:44:20,199
I won't let anyone

291
00:44:21,117 --> 00:44:22,660
touch even a hair on your head.

292
00:44:36,174 --> 00:44:37,758
I won't let them get the chance.

293
00:44:44,640 --> 00:44:45,641
You're right.

294
00:44:46,309 --> 00:44:47,977
They won't have a chance in hell.

295
00:45:08,122 --> 00:45:10,124
Jian, get down!

296
00:45:13,669 --> 00:45:14,753
Boom.

297
00:45:38,527 --> 00:45:42,031
Give them a warning shot, to wake them up.

298
00:45:44,992 --> 00:45:46,159
Woojin, drop down!

299
00:46:10,893 --> 00:46:12,686
Woojin. Woojin!

300
00:46:15,481 --> 00:46:17,400
It's okay. Just wait a second.

301
00:46:24,031 --> 00:46:25,283
Jeong Jian!

302
00:46:27,868 --> 00:46:29,912
I want Jeong Jian brought in alive.

303
00:46:31,956 --> 00:46:33,165
Jian, hey…

304
00:46:36,877 --> 00:46:37,962
Jeong Jian.

305
00:46:56,188 --> 00:46:57,648
That's your name, right?

306
00:47:00,318 --> 00:47:01,485
Jeong Jian?

307
00:47:05,614 --> 00:47:06,824
Uh-huh.

308
00:47:16,208 --> 00:47:18,127
Even your name is beautiful, Jian.

309
00:47:22,131 --> 00:47:23,674
I…

310
00:47:31,015 --> 00:47:32,683
Hey, didn't I promise you?

311
00:47:34,101 --> 00:47:35,561
Not a single hair.

312
00:47:36,145 --> 00:47:38,271
Not a single hair on your head.

313
00:47:44,445 --> 00:47:45,654
Let me just say…

314
00:47:48,324 --> 00:47:49,867
thanks for hanging out…

315
00:47:52,912 --> 00:47:54,622
with a hick like me.

316
00:48:14,016 --> 00:48:15,434
Woojin, hey!

317
00:48:16,185 --> 00:48:17,644
Don't close your eyes!

318
00:48:17,645 --> 00:48:19,229
No! You can't…

319
00:48:21,774 --> 00:48:23,109
You can't…

320
00:48:31,742 --> 00:48:33,452
Jeong Jinman!

321
00:48:36,622 --> 00:48:39,333
Jeong Jinman!

322
00:48:41,085 --> 00:48:48,007
Jeong Jinman!

323
00:49:44,356 --> 00:49:49,153
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

324
00:49:57,203 --> 00:49:58,662
BASED ON THE NOVEL BY KANG JI YOUNG
